-5900-95b7-4e118122dfc6"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405309 :tutorial/content "**6.1 Vector Fields**\n\nSource: [Macmillan Achieve](https://achieve.macmillanlearning.com/ihub/assessment/f188d950-dd73-11e0-9572-0800200c9a66/5a1db2a7-4295-4a4c-9dbb-ceb8b174a282/652f6185-14b0-408e-92fc-5cf7a73767b4?actualCourseId=5a1db2a7-4295-4a4c-9dbb-ceb8b174a282)\nDue: 2026-10-08\nImported: 2026-10-01 · 12 questions\n\nStudy answers, explanations, and reference graphics are authored additions to the linked source." :tutorial/id #uuid "53343a60-4e64-5900-95b7-4e118122dfc6" :tutorial/title "Assignment information"}] [[:answer/id #uuid "cfe1d858-fb08-5e8f-8cee-563c06bfdc25"] {:answer/feedback "A vector field assigns a vector to each point. The displayed sum is scalar; a three-dimensional vector field has the form $\\mathbf F=P\\mathbf i+Q\\mathbf j+R\\mathbf k$." :answer/id #uuid "cfe1d858-fb08-5e8f-8cee-563c06bfdc25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406230}] [[:answer/id #uuid "cede23f1-a796-5434-9ff2-e951f9f1d32f"] {:answer/feedback "Adding three scalar functions still gives a scalar. To obtain a vector field, use the functions as components: $\\mathbf F=\\langle P,Q,R\\rangle$." :answer/id #uuid "cede23f1-a796-5434-9ff2-e951f9f1d32f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406229}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "f760a9dc-d686-59fb-be09-2e9a14115c1f"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Adding three scalar functions still gives a scalar. To obtain a vector field, use the functions as components: $\\mathbf F=\\langle P,Q,R\\rangle$." :answer/id #uuid "cede23f1-a796-5434-9ff2-e951f9f1d32f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406229} {:answer/feedback "A vector field assigns a vector to each point. The displayed sum is scalar; a three-dimensional vector field has the form $\\mathbf F=P\\mathbf i+Q\\mathbf j+R\\mathbf k$." :answer/id #uuid "cfe1d858-fb08-5e8f-8cee-563c06bfdc25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406230}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406230} :answer-field/id #uuid "f760a9dc-d686-59fb-be09-2e9a14115c1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406311}] [[:question/id #uuid "6fc5de92-5e3b-5f47-bc37-7ab9debf2a81"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405396 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Adding three scalar functions still gives a scalar. To obtain a vector field, use the functions as components: $\\mathbf F=\\langle P,Q,R\\rangle$." :answer/id #uuid "cede23f1-a796-5434-9ff2-e951f9f1d32f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406229} {:answer/feedback "A vector field assigns a vector to each point. The displayed sum is scalar; a three-dimensional vector field has the form $\\mathbf F=P\\mathbf i+Q\\mathbf j+R\\mathbf k$." :answer/id #uuid "cfe1d858-fb08-5e8f-8cee-563c06bfdc25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406230}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406230} :answer-field/id #uuid "f760a9dc-d686-59fb-be09-2e9a14115c1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406311}] :question/id #uuid "6fc5de92-5e3b-5f47-bc37-7ab9debf2a81" :question/problem "Source question: 1.\n\n**Question 1**\n\nLet $P(x,y,z)$, $Q(x,y,z)$, and $R(x,y,z)$ be scalar functions on a region $E$. True or false: the formula $F(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)+Q(x,y,z)+R(x,y,z)$ defines a vector field on $E$." :question/worked-solution "A vector field assigns a vector to each point. The displayed sum is scalar; a three-dimensional vector field has the form $\\mathbf F=P\\mathbf i+Q\\mathbf j+R\\mathbf k$."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "bd551c10-e921-513b-bfba-3f9958869fab"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405396} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "bd551c10-e921-513b-bfba-3f9958869fab" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050418}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405637}] [[:answer/id #uuid "470edd10-4aa3-52da-8713-17356585e670"] {:answer/feedback "The gradient assigns the vector of partial derivatives to each point: $\\nabla f=\\langle f_x,f_y,f_z\\rangle$ in three dimensions. This is a vector field wherever those derivatives exist." :answer/id #uuid "470edd10-4aa3-52da-8713-17356585e670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405976}] [[:answer/id #uuid "bf9980ab-7810-5133-87c1-1a485924d069"] {:answer/feedback "Although $f$ is scalar-valued, its gradient collects its partial derivatives into a vector. The resulting assignment of a vector to each point is a vector field." :answer/id #uuid "bf9980ab-7810-5133-87c1-1a485924d069" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406201}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "f802ef4e-0bff-5fac-9205-d15549dbcbbb"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The gradient assigns the vector of partial derivatives to each point: $\\nabla f=\\langle f_x,f_y,f_z\\rangle$ in three dimensions. This is a vector field wherever those derivatives exist." :answer/id #uuid "470edd10-4aa3-52da-8713-17356585e670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405976} {:answer/feedback "Although $f$ is scalar-valued, its gradient collects its partial derivatives into a vector. The resulting assignment of a vector to each point is a vector field." :answer/id #uuid "bf9980ab-7810-5133-87c1-1a485924d069" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406201}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405976} :answer-field/id #uuid "f802ef4e-0bff-5fac-9205-d15549dbcbbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406313}] [[:question/id #uuid "780ba61c-d062-542b-ade5-ed2455551f56"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The gradient assigns the vector of partial derivatives to each point: $\\nabla f=\\langle f_x,f_y,f_z\\rangle$ in three dimensions. This is a vector field wherever those derivatives exist." :answer/id #uuid "470edd10-4aa3-52da-8713-17356585e670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405976} {:answer/feedback "Although $f$ is scalar-valued, its gradient collects its partial derivatives into a vector. The resulting assignment of a vector to each point is a vector field." :answer/id #uuid "bf9980ab-7810-5133-87c1-1a485924d069" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406201}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405976} :answer-field/id #uuid "f802ef4e-0bff-5fac-9205-d15549dbcbbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406313}] :question/id #uuid "780ba61c-d062-542b-ade5-ed2455551f56" :question/problem "Source question: 2.\n\n**Question 2**\n\nTrue or false: the gradient of a differentiable scalar function $f$ is a vector field." :question/worked-solution "The gradient assigns the vector of partial derivatives to each point: $\\nabla f=\\langle f_x,f_y,f_z\\rangle$ in three dimensions. This is a vector field wherever those derivatives exist."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "f8bfadfc-e70d-52fa-9c9d-58ff3e231e6b"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405423} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "f8bfadfc-e70d-52fa-9c9d-58ff3e231e6b" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050891}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405818}] [[:answer/id #uuid "d2c4bf4f-62bc-5b74-bc47-e4ec298654d0"] {:answer/feedback "The field $\\langle x,y\\rangle$ equals the position vector. Arrows point radially outward, with equal horizontal and vertical components where $x=y$, as shown." :answer/id #uuid "d2c4bf4f-62bc-5b74-bc47-e4ec298654d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "images/ce/ceba1e47532b41d313ce9ae2de01278ff3603154ffe070cd680a3859eab7de58.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406237}] [[:answer/id #uuid "72464a41-89fb-5d26-b827-b747a0817360"] {:answer/feedback "This graph points up and right even where coordinates are negative. For $\\langle x,y\\rangle$, each component must have the sign of its corresponding coordinate." :answer/id #uuid "72464a41-89fb-5d26-b827-b747a0817360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "images/0c/0c67b07111ce3e2d9d19586df1c6bf2b73c5c30c64c647013d9c1ebcbd5bc390.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406054}] [[:answer/id #uuid "7ef778d6-89b2-5217-8b8b-0cf0558470c0"] {:answer/feedback "This graph stretches the horizontal component relative to the vertical one. At $x=y\\ne0$, the required components are equal, so the arrow must lie at $45^\\circ$ to the axes." :answer/id #uuid "7ef778d6-89b2-5217-8b8b-0cf0558470c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "images/af/af33a889d5b3bc855f425cff0d88353af5a2d9910ceb3e98a89d8fb8888eba46.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406076}] [[:answer/id #uuid "1717fea9-ec21-503b-a8aa-877a297f7cc8"] {:answer/feedback "This graph stretches the vertical component relative to the horizontal one. The field $\\langle x,y\\rangle$ has equal components at $x=y$ and should point along that diagonal." :answer/id #uuid "1717fea9-ec21-503b-a8aa-877a297f7cc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "images/10/10c3b257b5adaa79ffdefae2a496ccdad15f46a8f70b0612471a7c9b53eb4677.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405878}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "064dd26c-2720-5640-996f-0a6fa292bb85"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This graph stretches the vertical component relative to the horizontal one. The field $\\langle x,y\\rangle$