#edb/ref 17592186406185}] :question/id #uuid "701c6ca9-db81-5c06-87d0-ae18e2e96b57" :question/problem "Source question: 12.\n\n**Question 12**\n\nA small mass $m$ (kg) produces gravitational potential $u=-Gm/r$, where $r$ is the distance from the mass in meters, $G=6.67\\times10^{-11}\\ \\mathrm{N\\,m^2/kg^2}$, and $\\mathbf r=x\\mathbf i+y\\mathbf j+z\\mathbf k$. If $\\mathbf g=-\\nabla u$, choose the expression for $\\mathbf g$." :question/worked-solution "Using $r=\\sqrt{x^2+y^2+z^2}$ gives $\\nabla(1/r)=-\\mathbf r/r^3$. Hence $\\nabla u=Gm\\mathbf r/r^3$ and $\\mathbf g=-Gm\\mathbf r/r^3$, directed toward the mass."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "9e8e7c89-c457-505e-8c6f-873fe67255ac"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405400} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "9e8e7c89-c457-505e-8c6f-873fe67255ac" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050149} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050891} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051090}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405543}] [[:step/id #uuid "73d94423-2860-50a9-b897-85a158061430"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405415 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405309} :step/id #uuid "73d94423-2860-50a9-b897-85a158061430" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405394}}] [[:step/id #uuid "6f22bf3d-00b0-5d4d-9c6d-5c35da0625c5"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405394 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405637} :step/id #uuid "6f22bf3d-00b0-5d4d-9c6d-5c35da0625c5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405354}}] [[:step/id #uuid "6433d198-5ddf-5bc6-9a85-2eda89bba82b"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405354 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405818} :step/id #uuid "6433d198-5ddf-5bc6-9a85-2eda89bba82b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405653}}] [[:step/id #uuid "c48d089b-9362-56a5-9e61-187732a48700"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405653 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405809} :step/id #uuid "c48d089b-9362-56a5-9e61-187732a48700" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405064}}] [[:step/id #uuid "048abeca-9232-55b4-866a-c7c4eb482243"] {:db/i