he linked source." :tutorial/id #uuid "e0c6591e-de96-5883-91c4-67813091a34a" :tutorial/title "Assignment information"}] [[:answer/id #uuid "bd899157-61fc-569f-8ca9-5f51811170ae"] {:answer/id #uuid "bd899157-61fc-569f-8ca9-5f51811170ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "2e^(4t)-2e^(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406198}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "99823897-20bb-5dab-9bd1-670456510695"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd899157-61fc-569f-8ca9-5f51811170ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "2e^(4t)-2e^(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406198}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406198} :answer-field/id #uuid "99823897-20bb-5dab-9bd1-670456510695" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406125}] [[:question/id #uuid "ae1c1214-2bed-5311-babc-b4998fb888c4"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405581 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd899157-61fc-569f-8ca9-5f51811170ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "2e^(4t)-2e^(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406198}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406198} :answer-field/id #uuid "99823897-20bb-5dab-9bd1-670456510695" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406125}] :question/id #uuid "ae1c1214-2bed-5311-babc-b4998fb888c4" :question/problem "[Open in WeBWorK](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_1/1)\n\n**Question 1**\n\nFind the function satisfying the differential equation\n\n$$\ny'-2y=4e^{4t}\n$$\n\nand $y(0)=0$.\n\n$y(t)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The integrating factor is $e^{-2t}$, so $(e^{-2t}y)\\prime=4e^{2t}$. Integrating gives $e^{-2t}y=2e^{2t}+C$. At $0$, $0=2+C$, hence $C=-2$. Differentiation gives $y\\prime-2y=4e^{4t}$."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "ee8e996b-8a4e-5d5a-bad4-5e805d0799f2"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405581} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "ee8e996b-8a4e-5d5a-bad4-5e805d0799f2" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048575} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049152}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405780}] [[:answer/id #uuid "4aaae060-8166-5f57-a1d6-5c6382ac1b3e"] {:answer/id #uuid "4aaae060-8166-5f57-a1d6-5c6382ac1b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "3t*e^t+9e^(5t)-5e^t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405987}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "4cfbfd64-3217-5f80-9a32-f68083f2ed3e"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4aaae060-8166-5f57-a1d6-5c6382ac1b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "3t*e^t+9e^(5t)-5e^t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405987}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405987} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cfbfd64-3217-5f80-9a32-f68083f2ed3e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405991}] [[:question/id #uuid "599b693d-6e02-5377-bef6-014fa6bb3f8c"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4aaae060-8166-5f57-a1d6-5c6382ac1b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "3t*e^t+9e^(5t)-5e^t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405987}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405987} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cfbfd64-3217-5f80-9a32-f68083f2ed3e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405991}] :question/id #uuid "599b693d-6e02-5377-bef6-014fa6bb3f8c" :question/problem "[Open in WeBWorK](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_1/2)\n\n**Question 2**\n\nSolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}-y=3e^t+36e^{5t}\n$$\n\nwith $y(0)=4$.\n\n$y(t)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Multiply by $e^{-t}$: $(e^{-t}y)\\prime=3+36e^{4t}$. Thus $e^{-t}y=3t+9e^{4t}+C$. At $0$, $4=9+C$, so $C=-5$. The resonant $3e^t$ forcing produces the $3te^t$ term."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "67cf92ba-f020-52d8-8b9d-91ba3fffa472"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405321} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "67cf92ba-f020-52d8-8b9d-91ba3fffa472" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048575} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049152}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405368}] [[:answer/id #uuid "84f3bcc9-f3e3-58e3-b68e-86f8f3141831"] {:answer/id #uuid "84f3bcc9-f3e3-58e3-b68e-86f8f3141831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "5+2e^(-sin(x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406094}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "78510d85-7c21-57cc-8912-8f9dc8404631"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84f3bcc9-f3e3-58e3-b68e-86f8f3141831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "5+2e^(-sin(x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406094}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406094} :answer-field/id #uuid "78510d85-7c21-57cc-8912-8f9dc8404631" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406061}] [[:question/id #uuid "b6875448-22bc-5b6c-8e17-3448ca6a39e2"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405615 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84f3bcc9-f3e3-58e3-b68e-86f8f3141831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "5+2e^(-sin(x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406094}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406094} :answer-field/id #uuid "78510d85-7c21-57cc-8912-8f9dc8404631" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406061}] :question/id #uuid "b6875448-22bc-5b6c-8e17-3448ca6a39e2" :question/problem "[Open in WeBWorK](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_1/3)\n\n**Question 3**\n\nFind the particular solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+y\\cos(x)=5\\cos(x)\n$$\n\nsatisfying the initial condition $y(0)=7$.\n\nYour answer should be a function of $x$.\n\n$y(x)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=y-5$. Then $u\\prime=-u\\cos x$, so $u=Ce^{-\\sin x}$. The initial value gives $C=2$. Check $y\\prime=-2\\cos x\\,e^{-\\sin x}$ and $y\\cos x=5\\cos x+2\\cos x\\,e^{-\\sin x}$; their sum is $5\\cos x$."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "da5939c4-e4df-53af-9400-a59c9098fbf1"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405615} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "da5939c4-e4df-53af-9400-a59c9098fbf1" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048703} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050911}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405722}] [[:answer/id #uuid "3bac3018-3229-5f6e-b232-f5b0a1ec62df"] {:answer/id #uuid "3bac3018-3229-5f6e-b232-f5b0a1ec62df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "x^(-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405943}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "68c25ce8-e599-5c4b-9822-28b84ba47ea0"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bac3018-3229-5f6e-b232-f5b0a1ec62df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "x^(-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405943}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405943} :answer-field/id #uuid "68c25ce8-e599-5c4b-9822-28b84ba47ea0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406037}] [[:question/id #uuid "774ef1c9-2be1-52e3-81f1-9b8fcb25c3b7"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405422 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bac3018-3229-5f6e-b232-f5b0a1ec62df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "x^(-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405943}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405943} :answer-field/id #uuid "68c25ce8-e599-5c4b-9822-28b84ba47ea0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406037}] :question/id #uuid "774ef1c9-2be1-52e3-81f1-9b8fcb25c3b7" :question/problem "**Question 4 — Part A**\n\nIdentify an integrating factor, $\\alpha(x)$.\n\n$\\alpha(x)=$ {{field-1}}, on $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Normalize first: $y\\prime-(9/x)y=-6$. Then $\\alpha=e^{\\int-9/x\\,dx}=x^{-9}$ on the positive interval containing $x=1$. Any nonzero constant multiple is also an integrating factor."}] [[:answer/id #uuid "28f1fe45-d5c8-5ace-af5c-e71851764b0c"] {:answer/id #uuid "28f1fe45-d5c8-5ace-af5c-e71851764b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "3x/4+C*x^9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405914}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "e6c0dd8c-effc-50fe-b32d-9f1edfe985a1"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28f1fe45-d5c8-5ace-af5c-e71851764b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "3x/4+C*x^9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405914}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405914} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6c0dd8c-effc-50fe-b32d-9f1edfe985a1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406274}] [[:question/id #uuid "26e6fa45-f47e-5e39-bff0-33cf4a2c6066"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28f1fe45-d5c8-5ace-af5c-e71851764b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "3x/4+C*x^9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405914}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405914} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6c0dd8c-effc-50fe-b32d-9f1edfe985a1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406274}] :question/id #uuid "26e6fa45-f47e-5e39-bff0-33cf4a2c6066" :question/problem "**Question 4 — Part B**\n\nFind a general solution of the differential equation $xy'=9y-6x$.\n\nYour “general solution” should be valid at every point in an open rectangle that includes the initial condition $(x,y)=(1,-4)$.\n\nUse $C$ for the arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=$ {{field-1}}, on $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "The product equation is $(x^{-9}y)\\prime=-6x^{-9}$. Integrating gives $x^{-9}y=(3/4)x^{-8}+C$, hence $y=(3/4)x+Cx^9$. The normalized coefficients are continuous on any open rectangle containing $(1,-4)$ whose $x$-range stays positive."}] [[:answer/id #uuid "7dbf00a3-a020-5475-b25d-ee6ffd8da635"] {:answer/id #uuid "7dbf00a3-a020-5475-b25d-ee6ffd8da635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "3x/4-19x^9/4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406073}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "f76813f9-ec42-5f4d-88e0-12fe5dbfab5a"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dbf00a3-a020-5475-b25d-ee6ffd8da635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "3x/4-19x^9/4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406073}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406073} :answer-field/id #uuid "f76813f9-ec42-5f4d-88e0-12fe5dbfab5a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406312}] [[:question/id #uuid "7614da17-ac59-5fb4-bc36-123b0e673350"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405420 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dbf00a3-a020-5475-b25d-ee6ffd8da635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "3x/4-19x^9/4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406073}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406073} :answer-field/id #uuid "f76813f9-ec42-5f4d-88e0-12fe5dbfab5a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406312}] :question/id #uuid "7614da17-ac59-5fb4-bc36-123b0e673350" :question/problem "**Question 4 — Part C**\n\nSolve the initial value problem.\n\n\n\nNote: You can earn partial credit on this problem.\n\n$y(x)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Insert $x=1$, $y=-4$ into $(3/4)x+Cx^9$: $C=-4-3/4=-19/4$. Substitution in $xy\\prime=9y-6x$ checks both sides as $(3/4)x-(171/4)x^9$."}] [[:step/id #uuid "70cec3ec-ccdd-50b9-8459-b78b529383af"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405403 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405422} :step/id #uuid "70cec3ec-ccdd-50b9-8459-b78b529383af" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405524}}] [[:step/id #uuid "99076efb-018d-59e1-aa5e-87e3037beab1"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405524 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405165} :step/id #uuid "99076efb-018d-59e1-aa5e-87e3037beab1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405769}}] [[:step/id #uuid "e92fea9e-4905-5db2-b39a-dcb875de387b"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405769 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405420} :step/id #uuid "e92fea9e-4905-5db2-b39a-dcb875de387b"}] [[:multistep/id #uuid "abcf5322-e31b-58c5-acc9-c0a106bdc0b3"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405577 :multistep/context "[Open in WeBWorK](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_1/4)\n\nIn this problem you will solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\nxy'=9y-6x,\\qquad y(1)=-4.\n$$" :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405403} :multistep/id #uuid "abcf5322-e31b-58c5-acc9-c0a106bdc0b3" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405403 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405422} :step/id #uuid "70cec3ec-ccdd-50b9-8459-b78b529383af" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405524}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405524 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405165} :step/id #uuid "99076efb-018d-59e1-aa5e-87e3037beab1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405769}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405769 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405420} :step/id #uuid "e92fea9e-4905-5db2-b39a-dcb875de387b"}]}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "ef25a050-05d7-5a1b-9216-560cd97b753c"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405577} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "ef25a050-05d7-5a1b-9216-560cd97b753c" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048575} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049487} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050614}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405785}] [[:answer/id #uuid "3c35c50e-6e16-5750-bbb6-21dbb8152fae"] {:answer/id #uuid "3c35c50e-6e16-5750-bbb6-21dbb8152fae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "(ln(x)-7/x+55)/(x+7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405946}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "275976cc-05f5-5848-b203-a7fc59374437"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c35c50e-6e16-5750-bbb6-21dbb8152fae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "(ln(x)-7/x+55)/(x+7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405946}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405946} :answer-field/id #uuid "275976cc-05f5-5848-b203-a7fc59374437" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405910}] [[:question/id #uuid "37d59c3a-3057-5e0d-a4b7-111ae8dd154d"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c35c50e-6e16-5750-bbb6-21dbb8152fae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "(ln(x)-7/x+55)/(x+7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405946}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405946} :answer-field/id #uuid "275976cc-05f5-5848-b203-a7fc59374437" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405910}] :question/id #uuid "37d59c3a-3057-5e0d-a4b7-111ae8dd154d" :question/problem "[Open in WeBWorK](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_1/5)\n\n**Question 5**\n\nSolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\ny'+\\frac{1}{x+7}y=x^{-2},\\qquad y(1)=6.\n$$\n\n$y(x)=$ {{field-1}}, on $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "An integrating factor on the interval containing $1$ is $x+7$. Thus $[(x+7)y]\\prime=(x+7)/x^2=1/x+7/x^2$, and $(x+7)y=\\ln x-7/x+C$. At $x=1$, $48=-7+C$, so $C=55$. The maximal coefficient interval containing the initial point is $(0,\\infty)$."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "4b0fa278-e621-5acd-855b-bea93a9113cf"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405214} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "4b0fa278-e621-5acd-855b-bea93a9113cf" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048575} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049487} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050614}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405285}] [[:answer/id #uuid "d150517c-19ae-5f24-9406-61abea29aa3c"] {:answer/id #uuid "d150517c-19ae-5f24-9406-61abea29aa3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "(5t^3+2)*e^(t^2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406233}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "94495ba8-8a29-5519-92cc-7d6c813b2233"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d150517c-19ae-5f24-9406-61abea29aa3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "(5t^3+2)*e^(t^2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406233}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406233} :answer-field/id #uuid "94495ba8-8a29-5519-92cc-7d6c813b2233" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406116}] [[:question/id #uuid "9d298f94-7673-5f4f-9204-6d79fb43db38"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d150517c-19ae-5f24-9406-61abea29aa3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "(5t^3+2)*e^(t^2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406233}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406233} :answer-field/id #uuid "94495ba8-8a29-5519-92cc-7d6c813b2233" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406116}] :question/id #uuid "9d298f94-7673-5f4f-9204-6d79fb43db38" :question/problem "[Open in WeBWorK](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_1/6)\n\n**Question 6**\n\nFind the function $y(t)$ that satisfies the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}-2ty=15t^2e^{t^2}\n$$\n\nand the condition $y(0)=2$.\n\n$y(t)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Multiply by $e^{-t^2}$ to get $(e^{-t^2}y)\\prime=15t^2$. Integration gives $e^{-t^2}y=5t^3+C$, and $y(0)=2$ gives $C=2$. Differentiating the final expression cancels the $2ty$ term and leaves $15t^2e^{t^2}$."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "05666c85-c7b9-5149-8738-3a739c3ab71a"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405541} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "05666c85-c7b9-5149-8738-3a739c3ab71a" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id 