n 2e Calculus, W.H. Freeman. Unlimited attempts, no incorrect-attempt penalty; up to 50 days late at a 2% daily penalty." :tutorial/id #uuid "1e23c156-59e0-56b1-bf9a-9ed09a3e3e67" :tutorial/title "Assignment information"}] [[:answer/id #uuid "ddabbd6e-2a42-5faa-afaa-93759b2170a7"] {:answer/id #uuid "ddabbd6e-2a42-5faa-afaa-93759b2170a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406259}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "c3c138d5-b52a-5be3-93f7-603eb04722a6"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddabbd6e-2a42-5faa-afaa-93759b2170a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406259}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406259} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3c138d5-b52a-5be3-93f7-603eb04722a6" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406209}] [[:question/id #uuid "d9765851-c4fa-5968-853c-7308afe7393b"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddabbd6e-2a42-5faa-afaa-93759b2170a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406259}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406259} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3c138d5-b52a-5be3-93f7-603eb04722a6" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406209}] :question/id #uuid "d9765851-c4fa-5968-853c-7308afe7393b" :question/problem "Source question: 1.\n\nEvaluate $\\oint_C3y\\,dx$ counterclockwise around the rectangle with vertices (0,0), (2,0), (2,6), (0,6).\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "$P=3y$, Q=0, so $Q_x-P_y=-3$. Green’s theorem gives −3 times the rectangle area 12, or −36. Directly, only the top horizontal side contributes: $\\int_2^0 18dx=-36$."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "93bd2316-ff02-5292-9fc0-a0d01f43d04b"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405719} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "93bd2316-ff02-5292-9fc0-a0d01f43d04b" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051076}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405514}] [[:answer/id #uuid "b4ed3be4-80cd-5af4-907a-a2cd207e43d6"] {:answer/id #uuid "b4ed3be4-80cd-5af4-907a-a2cd207e43d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406183}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "cdc79663-205a-5898-9e2f-1f413d36a28f"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4ed3be4-80cd-5af4-907a-a2cd207e43d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406183}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406183} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdc79663-205a-5898-9e2f-1f413d36a28f" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406225}] [[:question/id #uuid "fb2f69a0-f906-521b-9a80-545470b72fa5"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4ed3be4-80cd-5af4-907a-a2cd207e43d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406183}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406183} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdc79663-205a-5898-9e2f-1f413d36a28f" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406225}] :question/id #uuid "fb2f69a0-f906-521b-9a80-545470b72fa5" :question/problem "Source question: 2.\n\nEvaluate $\\oint_C2x\\,dy$ counterclockwise around the rectangle with vertices (0,0), (6,0), (6,2), (0,2).\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "$Q_x-P_y=2$. The enclosed area is 6·2=12, giving 24. The right side contributes $\\int_0^2 12dy=24$, and the left side contributes zero."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "cd3c23e0-e779-5100-9cce-fb8fe05ea74b"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405827} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "cd3c23e0-e779-5100-9cce-fb8fe05ea74b" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051076}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405679}] [[:answer/id #uuid "480601ae-51e7-5f5a-b625-7ca97efd3aa1"] {:answer/id #uuid "480601ae-51e7-5f5a-b625-7ca97efd3aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "-16\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405980}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "e6ceed08-2747-58a6-ae18-ad626498c36b"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "480601ae-51e7-5f5a-b625-7ca97efd3aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "-16\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405980}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405980} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6ceed08-2747-58a6-ae18-ad626498c36b" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406275}] [[:question/id #uuid "dd087078-f11d-57cf-a82c-11a691c0bd23"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405730 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "480601ae-51e7-5f5a-b625-7ca97efd3aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "-16\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405980}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405980} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6ceed08-2747-58a6-ae18-ad626498c36b" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406275}] :question/id #uuid "dd087078-f11d-57cf-a82c-11a691c0bd23" :question/problem "Source question: 3.\n\nEvaluate $\\oint_C8y(x^2+y^2)dx-8x(x^2+y^2)dy$ counterclockwise around the unit circle $x^2+y^2=1$.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "$Q_x-P_y=-32(x^2+y^2)$. Over the unit disk the double integral is $-32\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\int_0^1r^3drd\\theta=-16\\pi$. On the circle, direct substitution also gives the constant −8 in the θ integrand."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "e43f5dc3-1672-5878-bba4-6c06d49f6eb1"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405730} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "e43f5dc3-1672-5878-bba4-6c06d49f6eb1" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050338}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405760}] [[:answer/id #uuid "65b7a6c9-f0f9-5a99-8eb1-abe6e219bf55"] {:answer/id #uuid "65b7a6c9-f0f9-5a99-8eb1-abe6e219bf55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{39\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406031}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "4d7715cc-7e32-5e87-9be7-b41296808ba4"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65b7a6c9-f0f9-5a99-8eb1-abe6e219bf55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{39\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406031}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406031} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d7715cc-7e32-5e87-9be7-b41296808ba4" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405994}] [[:question/id #uuid "e7bdcb25-186c-54e2-bf5f-34faaeed962b"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405765 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65b7a6c9-f0f9-5a99-8eb1-abe6e219bf55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{39\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406031}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406031} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d7715cc-7e32-5e87-9be7-b41296808ba4" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405994}] :question/id #uuid "e7bdcb25-186c-54e2-bf5f-34faaeed962b" :question/problem "Source question: 4.\n\nEvaluate $\\oint_C(x^2-13y^3)dx+(x^2+y^2)dy$ counterclockwise around the unit circle $x^2+y^2=1$.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "$Q_x-P_y=2x+39y^2$. The odd term integrates to zero over the disk; $\\iint y^2dA=\\pi/4$, yielding 39π/4."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "231ef3d5-93fd-5d85-9133-54ad11c83683"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405765} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "231ef3d5-93fd-5d85-9133-54ad11c83683" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050338}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405148}] [[:answer/id #uuid "fa10f6d8-794b-5af9-b44b-c16c4baa20cf"] {:answer/id #uuid "fa10f6d8-794b-5af9-b44b-c16c4baa20cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac9{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406320}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "a8f2f977-3ad8-57b8-813a-6d73def8815e"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa10f6d8-794b-5af9-b44b-c16c4baa20cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac9{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406320}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406320} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8f2f977-3ad8-57b8-813a-6d73def8815e" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406160}] [[:question/id #uuid "c582ed14-fd82-598f-bd67-b4d2b53d152a"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405654 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa10f6d8-794b-5af9-b44b-c16c4baa20cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac9{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406320}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406320} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8f2f977-3ad8-57b8-813a-6d73def8815e" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406160}] :question/id #uuid "c582ed14-fd82-598f-bd67-b4d2b53d152a" :question/problem "Source question: 5.\n\nEvaluate $\\oint_C(5x^4-5y^2)dx+(7y-4xy)dy$ counterclockwise around the region bounded by $y=x^2$ and $y=\\sqrt x$.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "The curves intersect at x=0,1 and x²≤y≤√x. Since $Q_x-P_y=-4y+10y=6y$, the integral is $\\int_0^1\\int_{x^2}^{\\sqrt x}6y\\,dy\\,dx=3\\int_0^1(x-x^4)dx=9/10$."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "3ce2fe39-fb93-5f07-9341-02998105b7a5"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405654} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "3ce2fe39-fb93-5f07-9341-02998105b7a5" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051076}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405232}] [[:answer/id #uuid "378f0f81-9f6d-5911-80a7-408635c32bc5"] {:answer/id #uuid "378f0f81-9f6d-5911-80a7-408635c32bc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405935}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "be0f087d-cf55-53d8-81a1-6624290ea29f"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "378f0f81-9f6d-5911-80a7-408635c32bc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405935}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405935} :answer-field/id #uuid "be0f087d-cf55-53d8-81a1-6624290ea29f" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406200}] [[:question/id #uuid "af4dbefc-eb8c-5130-9503-7e037225ec74"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "378f0f81-9f6d-5911-80a7-408635c32bc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405935}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405935} :answer-field/id #uuid "be0f087d-cf55-53d8-81a1-6624290ea29f" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406200}] :question/id #uuid "af4dbefc-eb8c-5130-9503-7e037225ec74" :question/problem "Source question: 6.\n\nEvaluate $\\oint_C(4x^3-2x^2y)dx+9xy^2dy$ counterclockwise around the region bounded by $y=x^2$ and $x=y^2$.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "$Q_x-P_y=9y^2+2x^2$. Integrate over 0≤x≤1, x²≤y≤√x. Symmetry under swapping x and y makes both second moments equal: $\\iint_Rx^2dA=\\int_0^1(x^{5/2}-x^4)dx=3/35$. Thus the result is (9+2)3/35."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "6d7e7f26-f65a-52c5-835c-16e641946749"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405583} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "6d7e7f26-f65a-52c5-835c-16e641946749" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051076}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405385}] [[:answer/id #uuid "b46ac442-21ac-5191-8bdb-7bc28f76826e"] {:answer/id #uuid "b46ac442-21ac-5191-8bdb-7bc28f76826e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406180}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "c301c75b-856b-5a95-82dd-0fc20096614f"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b46ac442-21ac-5191-8bdb-7bc28f76826e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406180}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406180} :answer-field/id #uuid "c301c75b-856b-5a95-82dd-0fc20096614f" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406208}] [[:question/id #uuid "a5c60846-91e6-5bc4-ba34-d07324603b64"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405566 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b46ac442-21ac-5191-8bdb-7bc28f76826e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406180}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406180} :answer-field/id #uuid "c301c75b-856b-5a95-82dd-0fc20096614f" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406208}] :question/id #uuid "a5c60846-91e6-5bc4-ba34-d07324603b64" :question/problem "Source question: 7.\n\nFind $\\oint_C\\frac{y\\,dx-x\\,dy}{x^2+y^2}$ about $C:(x-8)^2+(y+7)^2=16$. Enter DNE if it does not exist.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "The disk has center (8,−7) and radius 4. The origin is outside, since its distance from the center is √113>4. The field is smooth on the disk and $Q_x-P_y=0$ there, so Green’s theorem gives zero. This value is unchanged by reversing orientation."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "b9d66075-219a-55df-aac0-190ab6c99923"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405566} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "b9d66075-219a-55df-aac0-190ab6c99923" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051076}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405626}] [[:answer/id #uuid "40ed2c73-c93b-5a23-9ab2-8ed7cde39a80"] {:answer/id #uuid "40ed2c73-c93b-5a23-9ab2-8ed7cde39a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "2(\\sqrt{11}-\\sqrt3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405959}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "f41aeb8a-602e-5f9e-b702-01e010461168"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40ed2c73-c93b-5a23-9ab2-8ed7cde39a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "2(\\sqrt{11}-\\sqrt3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405959}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405959} :answer-field/id #uuid "f41aeb8a-602e-5f9e-b702-01e010461168" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406302}] [[:question/id #uuid "2d791267-1db8-54f8-a188-c2f7c84f1df1"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40ed2c73-c93b-5a23-9ab2-8ed7cde39a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "2(\\sqrt{11}-\\sqrt3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405959}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405959} :answer-field/id #uuid "f41aeb8a-602e-5f9e-b702-01e010461168" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406302}] :question/id #uuid "2d791267-1db8-54f8-a188-c2f7c84f1df1" :question/problem "Source question: 8.\n\nUse **Green’s theorem** to find the area bounded by $y=1/\\sqrt{x-7}$, y=0, x=10, and x=18.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "Choose P=−y,Q=0, giving $Q_x-P_y=1$ and $A=-\\oint_Cy\\,dx$ for positive orientation. Only the upper boundary contributes; it is traversed from x=18 to 10. Hence $A=\\int_{10}^{18}(x-7)^{-1/2}dx=2(\\sqrt{11}-\\sqrt3)$."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "3507a79d-015b-52fa-9724-eae6fd4ab55f"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405185} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "3507a79d-015b-52fa-9724-eae6fd4ab55f" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050573}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405207}] [[:answer/id #uuid "32cda14b-ce4a-56dc-bfae-96c9f5a5d628"] {:answer/id #uuid "32cda14b-ce4a-56dc-bfae-96c9f5a5d628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405931}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "6f55237d-021e-599a-893a-1249d3ba6ccf"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32cda14b-ce4a-56dc-bfae-96c9f5a5d628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405931}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405931} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f55237d-021e-599a-893a-1249d3ba6ccf" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406049}] [[:question/id #uuid "833b6edc-bdc6-5193-a541-4ce8a5225340"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405459 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32cda14b-ce4a-56dc-bfae-96c9f5a5d628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405931}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405931} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f55237d-021e-599a-893a-1249d3ba6ccf" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406049}] :question/id #uuid "833b6edc-bdc6-5193-a541-4ce8a5225340" :question/problem "Source question: 9.\n\nThe folium of Descartes is parameterized by $x(t)=8t/(1+t^3)$, $y(t)=8t^2/(1+t^3)$. Use **Green’s theorem** to find the area enclosed by its loop.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise loop runs from t=0 to t→∞. Green’s area formula gives $A=\\frac12\\int_0^\\infty(xy′-yx′)dt=32\\int_0^\\infty t^2/(1+t^3)^2dt$. With u=1+t³ this is $\\frac{32}{3}\\int_1^\\infty u^{-2}du=32/3$."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "4d51339a-cc1f-53f3-9331-eb933dc2a018"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405459} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "4d51339a-cc1f-53f3-9331-eb933dc2a018" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050573}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405290}] [[:answer/id #uuid "a0506954-1fb4-5d2a-ab16-467353c99fd7"] {:answer/id #uuid "a0506954-1fb4-5d2a-ab16-467353c99fd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406142}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "63641206-34f8-5567-94ea-f671b3f5c470"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0506954-1fb4-5d2a-ab16-467353c99fd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406142}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406142} :answer-field/id #uuid "63641206-34f8-5567-94ea-f671b3f5c470" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406028}] [[:question/id #uuid "96e3d9de-8d87-5c0f-8f11-82863c4ad4c0"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405521 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0506954-1fb4-5d2a-ab16-467353c99fd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406142}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406142} :answer-field/id #uuid "63641206-34f8-5567-94ea-f671b3f5c470" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406028}] :question/id #uuid "96e3d9de-8d87-5c0f-8f11-82863c4ad4c0" :question/problem "Source question: 10.\n\nUse **Green’s theorem** to find the work of $\\mathbf F=5x\\mathbf i+2y^2\\mathbf j$ along $x=t,y=t^2$, $0\\le t\\le3$, then back to (0,0) along $x=t,y=3t$.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "The return line is traversed with t decreasing from 3 to 0. Green’s theorem gives $\\iint_R(Q_x-P_y)dA=0$, since both cross partials vanish. A check is the global potential $5x^2/2+2y^3/3$: its net change around the closed path is zero."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "d04819fe-1fd4-58fc-80dc-e7c819f1bef7"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405521} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "d04819fe-1fd4-58fc-80dc-e7c819f1bef7" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051076}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405691}] [[:answer/id #uuid "d24fd8a5-0c9a-5d51-a18e-43d926a86252"] {:answer/id #uuid "d24fd8a5-0c9a-5d51-a18e-43d926a86252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "-\\frac{45\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406234}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "20e542bd-e4cd-523c-a8e2-a899297a6c41"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d24fd8a5-0c9a-5d51-a18e-43d926a86252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "-\\frac{45\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406234}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406234} :answer-field/id #uuid "20e542bd-e4cd-523c-a8e2-a899297a6c41" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405897}] [[:question/id #uuid "fb56bd98-3f47-577d-b704-676611da0785"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d24fd8a5-0c9a-5d51-a18e-43d926a86252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "-\\frac{45\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406234}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406234} :answer-field/id #uuid "20e542bd-e4cd-523c-a8e2-a899297a6c41" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405897}] :question/id #uuid "fb56bd98-3f47-577d-b704-676611da0785" :question/problem "Source question: 11.\n\nFind $\\oint_C y^3dx-x^3dy$, where C is the boundary of the region between $x^2+y^2=4$ and $x^2+y^2=1$.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the standard positive boundary orientation (outer circle counterclockwise, inner circle clockwise), $Q_x-P_y=-3r^2$. Thus $I=-3\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\int_1^2r^3drd\\theta=-45\\pi/2$. The source does not explicitly specify orientation; reversing the full boundary changes the sign."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "4152b34c-8d3f-5593-a073-50b1e7afd378"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405828} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "4152b34c-8d3f-5593-a073-50b1e7afd378" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050566}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405251}] [[:answer/id #uuid "5d8e2895-863d-5b39-a612-d1aa2e3a12d3"] {:answer/id #uuid "5d8e2895-863d-5b39-a612-d1aa2e3a12d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{2197}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406014}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "86ec4b24-b565-52c5-b487-dfb53b6b0462"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d8e2895-863d-5b39-a612-d1aa2e3a12d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{2197}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406014}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406014} :answer-field/id #uuid "86ec4b24-b565-52c5-b487-dfb53b6b0462" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406097}] [[:question/id #uuid "127a5831-49e6-57dd-9d16-925eb9ca8b6a"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405101 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d8e2895-863d-5b39-a612-d1aa2e3a12d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{2197}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406014}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406014} :answer-field/id #uuid "86ec4b24-b565-52c5-b487-dfb53b6b0462" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406097}] :question/id #uuid "127a5831-49e6-57dd-9d16-925eb9ca8b6a" :question/problem "Source question: 12.\n\nUse **Green’s theorem** to find the area bounded by $y=x^2$ and $y=x+42$.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "The intersections solve x²−x−42=(x−7)(x+6)=0. Use $A=-\\oint_Cy\\,dx$ with positive orientation: lower parabola from −6 to 7, upper line from 7 to −6. Then $A=\\int_{-6}^7(x+42-x^2)dx=2197/6$."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "3c978f8d-d0f0-5398-9e77-0fc642ab3f19"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405101} :assigned-proble