field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa5e9de3-7aa2-558e-a7b4-a862b85fdbf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "f" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406162}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406162} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0688b7a-90f9-5f3d-9cf7-daaf62d3a9f6" :answer-field/key "plot-b" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406173} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88b6fc19-d548-5a32-8989-8c0fdadc06eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406100}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406100} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb0611f9-13bf-556a-a8aa-e40729d28be8" :answer-field/key "plot-d" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406221} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc4ff9e-050d-5a95-b785-dd9051e824c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405891}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405891} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6bd1ff4-957c-5da0-8bcc-9b65c3be81fa" :answer-field/key "plot-e" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406246} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb8bd873-c1a5-51f2-9f1b-ed3dad940eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406223}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406223} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4c0ca37-0193-55c9-ba66-282ac52afb17" :answer-field/key "plot-a" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406270} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6996da6-a54d-5266-922a-f00aa53fe057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406308}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406308} :answer-field/id #uuid "f513e12b-55f7-5cb0-a789-cce200ba11fb" :answer-field/key "plot-f" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406304}] :question/id #uuid "45d8f0f6-281d-501a-8a32-10aa83f6f4de" :question/problem "Source question: 2, PDF page 3.\n\nLet $\\mathbf F=\\langle x,y\\rangle$, $\\mathbf G=\\langle-y,x\\rangle$, and $\\mathbf H=\\langle x,-y\\rangle$. Match plots A–F to (a)–(f). Some plots are scaled for clarity.\n\n![Vector field plots A–F](images/ba/bab4c1e1ab7751751726e766e5fadef2c28e3dce5665f44345eb3315c65355cd.png)\n\n(a) $-\\mathbf G$; (b) $\\mathbf G-\\mathbf F$; (c) $\\mathbf F+\\mathbf H$; (d) $\\mathbf G+\\mathbf H$; (e) $\\mathbf H$; (f) $\\mathbf G+\\mathbf F$.\n\nPlot A: {{plot-a}}.\n\nPlot B: {{plot-b}}.\n\nPlot C: {{plot-c}}.\n\nPlot D: {{plot-d}}.\n\nPlot E: {{plot-e}}.\n\nPlot F: {{plot-f}}." :question/worked-solution "A–e, B–f, C–c, D–d, E–b, F–a. Compute components: $-G=(y,-x)$ is clockwise; $G-F=(-x-y,x-y)$ rotates inward; $F+H=(2x,0)$ is horizontal; $G+H=(x-y,x-y)$ has equal components; $H=(x,-y)$ is a saddle; $G+F=(x-y,x+y)$ rotates outward. Check signs on each axis to distinguish B from E."}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "07e95435-5f31-518b-9665-76645c61ebd7"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405266} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "07e95435-5f31-518b-9665-76645c61ebd7" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048923} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050142}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405076}] [[:question/id #uuid "2699c995-b9b2-5d31-ac4d-2299df3907b0"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405163 :question/id #uuid "2699c995-b9b2-5d31-ac4d-2299df3907b0" :question/problem "**(a)** Find every point at which the field is orthogonal or tangent to the curve.\n\n$\\mathbf F=\\langle1,0\\rangle$, $C: y-x^2=-1$." :question/worked-solution "**tangent-and-orthogonal:** Tangent: $(0,-1)$. Orthogonal: no points.\n\nA tangent is $T=(1,2x)$. The determinant of F and T is 2x, so tangency requires x=0. But $F\\cdot T=1$, so orthogonality is impossible."}] [[:question/id #uuid "26ee22cb-47df-5d06-a7c5-e7426f0949fb"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405166 :question/id #uuid "26ee22cb-47df-5d06-a7c5-e7426f0949fb" :question/problem "**(b)** Find every point at which the field is orthogonal or tangent to the curve.\n\n$\\mathbf F=\\langle y,-x\\rangle$, $C: y-x^2=1$." :question/worked-solution "**tangent-and-orthogonal:** Tangent: $(0,1)$. Orthogonal: $(1,2)$ and $(-1,2)$.\n\nOn the curve, $F=(x^2+1,-x)$ and $T=(1,2x)$. Their determinant is $x(2x^2+3)$, which vanishes only at x=0. Their dot product is $1-x^2$, so orthogonality occurs at x=±1, y=2."}] [[:question/id #uuid "aa8cad15-5ba4-5bc8-8d05-7b4753877e98"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405573 :question/id #uuid "aa8cad15-5ba4-5bc8-8d05-7b4753877e98" :question/problem "**(c)** Find every point at which the field is orthogonal or tangent to the curve.\n\n$\\mathbf F=\\langle y,x\\rangle$, $C: x^2+y^2=4$." :question/worked-solution "**tangent-and-orthogonal:** Tangent: $(\\pm2,0),(0,\\pm2)$. Orthogonal: all four $(\\pm\\sqrt2,\\pm\\sqrt2)$ with signs independent.\n\nUse the nonzero tangent $T=(-y,x)$. Tangency requires the determinant $2xy=0$; intersect with the circle to get its four axis intercepts. Orthogonality requires $F\\cdot T=x^2-y^2=0$; then x²=y²=2."}] [[:step/id #uuid "1f97ad93-73d0-589f-a7f3-5e40b21033e3"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405132 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405163} :step/id #uuid "1f97ad93-73d0-589f-a7f3-5e40b21033e3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405670}}] [[:step/id #uuid "c8c13483-7faa-568a-8c5b-3727a23f01b7"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405670 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405166} :step/id #uuid "c8c13483-7faa-568a-8c5b-3727a23f01b7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405105}}] [[:step/id #uuid "13d64c2a-3e82-58e2-8312-f805798f9188"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405105 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405573} :step/id #uuid "13d64c2a-3e82-58e2-8312-f805798f9188"}] [[:multistep/id #uuid "41b18ac5-4e50-5775-a25b-c5b24a12bf68"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405254 :multistep/context "Source question: 3(a)–(c), PDF page 4." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405132} :multistep/id #uuid "41b18ac5-4e50-5775-a25b-c5b24a12bf68" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405105 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405573} :step/id #uuid "13d64c2a-3e82-58e2-8312-f805798f9188"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405132 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405163} :step/id #uuid "1f97ad93-73d0-589f-a7f3-5e40b21033e3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405670}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405670 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405166} :step/id #uuid "c8c13483-7faa-568a-8c5b-3727a23f01b7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405105}}]}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "43336226-8048-5d54-b813-998eb740ce17"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405254} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "43336226-8048-5d54-b813-998eb740ce17" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048960} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049721}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405258}] [[:answer/id #uuid "fea44fc7-249f-5f17-be2b-f237eb092717"] {:answer/id #uuid "fea44fc7-249f-5f17-be2b-f237eb092717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{\\langle3-x,2-y\\rangle}{\\sqrt{(3-x)^2+(2-y)^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406334}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "039ead5f-991d-5e42-b1c2-42c605f4437b"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fea44fc7-249f-5f17-be2b-f237eb092717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{\\langle3-x,2-y\\rangle}{\\sqrt{(3-x)^2+(2-y)^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406334}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406334} :answer-field/id #uuid "039ead5f-991d-5e42-b1c2-42c605f4437b" :answer-field/key "field" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405842}] [[:question/id #uuid "4e6407c6-2c27-58f3-aad5-e22d8eba63d8"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405293 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fea44fc7-249f-5f17-be2b-f237eb092717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{\\langle3-x,2-y\\rangle}{\\sqrt{(3-x)^2+(2-y)^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406334}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406334} :answer-field/id #uuid "039ead5f-991d-5e42-b1c2-42c605f4437b" :answer-field/key "field" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405842}] :question/id #uuid "4e6407c6-2c27-58f3-aad5-e22d8eba63d8" :question/problem "**(a)** Find the unique two-dimensional field that is undefined at (3,2), unit everywhere else, and points toward (3,2).\n\n$\\mathbf F(x,y)=$ {{field}}." :question/worked-solution "The displacement toward (3,2) is $(3-x,2-y)$. Divide by its positive length. The denominator vanishes exactly at (3,2), and the resulting magnitude is 1."}] [[:answer/id #uuid "462ca8e6-2b37-5a41-8303-e9041b671a6f"] {:answer/id #uuid "462ca8e6-2b37-5a41-8303-e9041b671a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{\\langle x-y,y-x\\rangle}{\\sqrt2\\,|x-y|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405975}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "f0b47a40-9988-57be-b85b-26b758da5ee4"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "462ca8e6-2b37-5a41-8303-e9041b671a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{\\langle x-y,y-x\\rangle}{\\sqrt2\\,|x-y|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405975}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405975} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0b47a40-9988-57be-b85b-26b758da5ee4" :answer-field/key "field" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406294}] [[:question/id #uuid "706cd50f-7f72-519c-9239-88dfe94c53eb"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405402 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "462ca8e6-2b37-5a41-8303-e9041b671a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{\\langle x-y,y-x\\rangle}{\\sqrt2\\,|x-y|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405975}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405975} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0b47a40-9988-57be-b85b-26b758da5ee4" :answer-field/key "field" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406294}] :question/id #uuid "706cd50f-7f72-519c-9239-88dfe94c53eb" :question/problem "**(b)** Find the unique two-dimensional field that is undefined on y=x, unit everywhere else, and points away from and orthogonal to y=x.\n\n$\\mathbf F(x,y)=$ {{field}}." :question/worked-solution "The closest point on the line is $((x+y)/2,(x+y)/2)$. The displacement away from that point is proportional to $(x-y,y-x)$, perpendicular to (1,1). Its length is $\\sqrt2|x-y|$. Normalize; the sign automatically reverses across the line."}] [[:step/id #uuid "26127704-1090-55bf-b512-78ba7c6f5ed7"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405159 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405293} :step/id #uuid "26127704-1090-55bf-b512-78ba7c6f5ed7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405767}}] [[:step/id #uuid "e8aa47a9-f820-5e46-b015-e8fc4c816e0b"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405767 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405402} :step/id #uuid "e8aa47a9-f820-5e46-b015-e8fc4c816e0b"}] [[:multistep/id #uuid "0fde5e2a-8723-5760-981f-9e2e9cb2414c"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405095 :multistep/context "Source question: 4(a)–(b), PDF page 5." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405159} :multistep/id #uuid "0fde5e2a-8723-5760-981f-9e2e9cb2414c" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405159 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405293} :step/id #uuid "26127704-1090-55bf-b512-78ba7c6f5ed7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405767}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405767 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405402} :step/id #uuid "e8aa47a9-f820-5e46-b015-e8fc4c816e0b"}]}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "7e5ec52f-a8e3-522d-b0a7-9a4a87670d0a"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405095} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "7e5ec52f-a8e3-522d-b0a7-9a4a87670d0a" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049366}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405445}] [[:question/id #uuid "9d24bd49-2c8c-554c-82b9-08aca2bb217e"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405540 :question/id #uuid "9d24bd49-2c8c-554c-82b9-08aca2bb217e" :question/problem "**(a)** Confirm that the given curve is a flow curve for the field.\n\n$\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle\\cos t,\\sin t,e^t\\rangle$, $\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=\\langle-y,x,z\\rangle$." :question/worked-solution "**verification:** $\\mathbf r\\prime(t)=\\langle-\\sin t,\\cos t,e^t\\rangle=\\mathbf F(\\cos t,\\sin t,e^t)$ for every real t.\n\nDifferentiate each coordinate of r and separately substitute r into F. Equality of all three components proves $\\mathbf r\\prime=\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r)$ on the stated domain."}] [[:question/id #uuid "e318db23-2661-528d-a7d7-06a3c8e1754d"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405756 :question/id #uuid "e318db23-2661-528d-a7d7-06a3c8e1754d" :question/problem "**(b)** Confirm that the given curve is a flow curve for the field.\n\n$\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle e^{3t},1/t,\\ln t\\rangle$ for $t>0$, $\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=\\langle3x,-y^2,y\\rangle$." :question/worked-solution "**verification:** $\\mathbf r\\prime(t)=\\langle3e^{3t},-1/t^2,1/t\\rangle=\\mathbf F(e^{3t},1/t,\\ln t)$ for t>0.\n\nDifferentiate each coordinate of r and separately substitute r into F. Equality of all three components proves $\\mathbf r\\prime=\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r)$ on the stated domain."}] [[:step/id #uuid "8e2a8e32-f1c0-576d-85b8-630cda12606a"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405499 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405540} :step/id #uuid "8e2a8e32-f1c0-576d-85b8-630cda12606a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405426}}] [[:step/id #uuid "79136b16-3c28-5c70-8b52-16d8f5df9ad7"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405426 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405756} :step/id #uuid "79136b16-3c28-5c70-8b52-16d8f5df9ad7"}] [[:multistep/id #uuid "bf09e225-dc63-563c-8b55-4c55af8a069a"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405642 :multistep/context "Source question: 5(a)–(b), PDF page 6." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405499} :multistep/id #uuid "bf09e225-dc63-563c-8b55-4c55af8a069a" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb