left\\langle\\frac{-y}{x^2+y^2},\\frac{x}{x^2+y^2}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406267}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406267} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc591ebf-d623-583f-9058-df4dc5937a89" :answer-field/key "gradient" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406195}] [[:answer/id #uuid "3ab7a88b-b06d-5ea8-80b8-de2ff0953d30"] {:answer/id #uuid "3ab7a88b-b06d-5ea8-80b8-de2ff0953d30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "All points with x=0." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405940}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "7f66ba86-8c3d-5697-8255-1e95ed120836"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ab7a88b-b06d-5ea8-80b8-de2ff0953d30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "All points with x=0." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405940}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405940} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f66ba86-8c3d-5697-8255-1e95ed120836" :answer-field/key "excluded" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406079}] [[:question/id #uuid "1cea1af1-963f-518b-b83a-160d05ee007e"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405123 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ab7a88b-b06d-5ea8-80b8-de2ff0953d30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "All points with x=0." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405940}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405940} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f66ba86-8c3d-5697-8255-1e95ed120836" :answer-field/key "excluded" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e10cbc5b-f9c7-5ab5-8d41-936ce2db2334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\left\\langle\\frac{-y}{x^2+y^2},\\frac{x}{x^2+y^2}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406267}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406267} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc591ebf-d623-583f-9058-df4dc5937a89" :answer-field/key "gradient" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406195}] :question/id #uuid "1cea1af1-963f-518b-b83a-160d05ee007e" :question/problem "**(b)** $\\phi=\\tan^{-1}(y/x)$. Find its gradient field and the points excluded from its domain.\n\nGradient: {{gradient}}.\n\nExcluded points: {{excluded}}." :question/worked-solution "The chain rule gives $\\phi_x=(-y/x^2)/(1+y^2/x^2)$ and $\\phi_y=(1/x)/(1+y^2/x^2)$. Simplification gives the displayed gradient, but the original potential requires x≠0. Do not enlarge its domain just because the simplified formula exists elsewhere."}] [[:answer/id #uuid "5e0d688c-a983-5188-b566-30031343de77"] {:answer/id #uuid "5e0d688c-a983-5188-b566-30031343de77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\left\\langle\\frac{-y}{x^2+y^2},\\frac{x}{x^2+y^2}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406017}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "cd7f6cec-5c9c-58ef-8fc6-1f9623c0db8f"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e0d688c-a983-5188-b566-30031343de77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\left\\langle\\frac{-y}{x^2+y^2},\\frac{x}{x^2+y^2}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406017}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406017} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd7f6cec-5c9c-58ef-8fc6-1f9623c0db8f" :answer-field/key "gradient" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406224}] [[:answer/id #uuid "fc6aa6e4-87a9-5a74-a5d6-25c60523b046"] {:answer/id #uuid "fc6aa6e4-87a9-5a74-a5d6-25c60523b046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "All points with y=0." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406329}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "3b6606ce-843b-5f31-b9da-7cb4875e8f5a"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc6aa6e4-87a9-5a74-a5d6-25c60523b046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "All points with y=0." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406329}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406329} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b6606ce-843b-5f31-b9da-7cb4875e8f5a" :answer-field/key "excluded" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405942}] [[:question/id #uuid "dd682f09-fbef-5c58-90e4-4d25459c6e1c"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405732 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc6aa6e4-87a9-5a74-a5d6-25c60523b046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "All points with y=0." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406329}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406329} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b6606ce-843b-5f31-b9da-7cb4875e8f5a" :answer-field/key "excluded" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405942} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e0d688c-a983-5188-b566-30031343de77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\left\\langle\\frac{-y}{x^2+y^2},\\frac{x}{x^2+y^2}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406017}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406017} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd7f6cec-5c9c-58ef-8fc6-1f9623c0db8f" :answer-field/key "gradient" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406224}] :question/id #uuid "dd682f09-fbef-5c58-90e4-4d25459c6e1c" :question/problem "**(c)** $\\phi=\\frac\\pi2-\\tan^{-1}(x/y)$. Find its gradient field and the points excluded from its domain.\n\nGradient: {{gradient}}.\n\nExcluded points: {{excluded}}." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the negative arctangent: $\\phi_x=-(1/y)/(1+x^2/y^2)$ and $\\phi_y=(x/y^2)/(1+x^2/y^2)$. The gradient agrees with part (b) where both potentials are defined, but this potential requires y≠0."}] [[:answer/id #uuid "64951ee8-437a-512e-84bc-abb08975a79c"] {:answer/id #uuid "64951ee8-437a-512e-84bc-abb08975a79c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{\\langle x,y,z\\rangle}{x^2+y^2+z^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406030}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "577cfbc7-5a0a-5653-a538-4aa48090e001"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64951ee8-437a-512e-84bc-abb08975a79c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{\\langle x,y,z\\rangle}{x^2+y^2+z^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406030}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406030} :answer-field/id #uuid "577cfbc7-5a0a-5653-a538-4aa48090e001" :answer-field/key "gradient" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406010}] [[:answer/id #uuid "5f63d8fb-e582-5392-bbb3-6ef6bb2ca0c5"] {:answer/id #uuid "5f63d8fb-e582-5392-bbb3-6ef6bb2ca0c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "Only (0,0,0)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406021}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "3adea267-8efc-5c08-b759-21bf23a31281"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f63d8fb-e582-5392-bbb3-6ef6bb2ca0c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "Only (0,0,0)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406021}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406021} :answer-field/id #uuid "3adea267-8efc-5c08-b759-21bf23a31281" :answer-field/key "excluded" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405941}] [[:question/id #uuid "f374f30e-0227-5a2c-bc70-67159330b8cb"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f63d8fb-e582-5392-bbb3-6ef6bb2ca0c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "Only (0,0,0)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406021}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406021} :answer-field/id #uuid "3adea267-8efc-5c08-b759-21bf23a31281" :answer-field/key "excluded" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405941} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64951ee8-437a-512e-84bc-abb08975a79c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\frac{\\langle x,y,z\\rangle}{x^2+y^2+z^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406030}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406030} :answer-field/id #uuid "577cfbc7-5a0a-5653-a538-4aa48090e001" :answer-field/key "gradient" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406010}] :question/id #uuid "f374f30e-0227-5a2c-bc70-67159330b8cb" :question/problem "**(d)** $\\phi=\\frac{\\ln(x^2+y^2+z^2)}2$. Find its gradient field and the points excluded from its domain.\n\nGradient: {{gradient}}.\n\nExcluded points: {{excluded}}." :question/worked-solution "The logarithm requires $x^2+y^2+z^2>0$. Differentiating gives $\\phi_x=x/(x^2+y^2+z^2)$ and analogous y,z components. No additional points are lost."}] [[:step/id #uuid "b52ab28e-ea5b-5852-9018-db7608132ecc"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405607 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405659} :step/id #uuid "b52ab28e-ea5b-5852-9018-db7608132ecc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405283}}] [[:step/id #uuid "4a58d696-61d2-5b7a-9601-2438620bbaa3"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405283 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405123} :step/id #uuid "4a58d696-61d2-5b7a-9601-2438620bbaa3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405766}}] [[:step/id #uuid "e878eaca-e204-54ad-8ae4-99bb9c46dadc"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405766 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405732} :step/id #uuid "e878eaca-e204-54ad-8ae4-99bb9c46dadc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405364}}] [[:step/id #uuid "666ab9de-2eb0-59e8-ba62-b808e1a751c2"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405364 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405805} :step/id #uuid "666ab9de-2eb0-59e8-ba62-b808e1a751c2"}] [[:multistep/id #uuid "3cc0e38b-edca-5f6c-857c-76d6bc2e6e13"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405231 :multistep/context "Source question: 1(a)–(d), PDF page 2.\n\nThe gradient’s domain is the potential’s domain minus any additional points where a partial derivative does not exist." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405607} :multistep/id #uuid "3cc0e38b-edca-5f6c-857c-76d6bc2e6e13" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405283 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405123} :step/id #uuid "4a58d696-61d2-5b7a-9601-2438620bbaa3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405766}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405364 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405805} :step/id #uuid "666ab9de-2eb0-59e8-ba62-b808e1a751c2"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405607 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405659} :step/id #uuid "b52ab28e-ea5b-5852-9018-db7608132ecc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405283}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405766 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405732} :step/id #uuid "e878eaca-e204-54ad-8ae4-99bb9c46dadc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405364}}]}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "267f9dc5-5178-52db-9112-19f650d22d08"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405231} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "267f9dc5-5178-52db-9112-19f650d22d08" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050149} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050418} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050891}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405162}] [[:question/id #uuid "bf36cced-5fd5-5019-a7a0-eab3ed76260a"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405644 :question/id #uuid "bf36cced-5fd5-5019-a7a0-eab3ed76260a" :question/problem "**(a)** Draw F and C in the same coordinate axes." :question/worked-solution "**drawing:** Draw the radius-a circle centered at the origin. At every nonzero point, draw an equal-length arrow pointing radially outward; no field vector exists at the origin. At (a,0), (0,a), (−a,0), (0,−a), arrows point right, up, left, down.\n\n![Authored radial field reference](images/a8/a81e47b17c286f2bbb3393045774604a075906fc99c8a42c6562c95605d6c64b.png)\n\nNormalization makes every field vector length 1. Its direction is the position vector (x,y). The reference diagram uses uniformly scaled arrows and labels distance in units of a."}] [[:answer/id #uuid "4996ae5b-31b5-5deb-aa6f-7b3c3974a861"] {:answer/id #uuid "4996ae5b-31b5-5deb-aa6f-7b3c3974a861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\langle2x,2y\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405984}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "fa01be6a-80d9-5bb9-a9a2-c1aa3fc1f50b"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4996ae5b-31b5-5deb-aa6f-7b3c3974a861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\langle2x,2y\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405984}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405984} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa01be6a-80d9-5bb9-a9a2-c1aa3fc1f50b" :answer-field/key "gradient" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406318}] [[:question/id #uuid "c70ca3f2-a964-523d-9c4f-6df57fea40bb"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4996ae5b-31b5-5deb-aa6f-7b3c3974a861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\langle2x,2y\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405984}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405984} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa01be6a-80d9-5bb9-a9a2-c1aa3fc1f50b" :answer-field/key "gradient" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406318}] :question/id #uuid "c70ca3f2-a964-523d-9c4f-6df57fea40bb" :question/problem "**(b)** Find $\\nabla\\eta(x,y)$. Notice that η is not a potential for F, but its gradient is parallel to F and points in the same direction.\n\nGradient: {{gradient}}." :question/worked-solution "$\\eta_x=2x$ and $\\eta_y=2y$, so $\\nabla\\eta=2\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}\\,F$ at every nonzero point. The scalar is positive; it is not identically 1, so η is not a potential for F."}] [[:question/id #uuid "c6899113-5e70-523e-b4e3-f94c34a9f739"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405662 :question/id #uuid "c6899113-5e70-523e-b4e3-f94c34a9f739" :question/problem "**(c)** Conclude that at every point on C, F is orthogonal to C." :question/worked-solution "**proof:** C is the level curve $\\eta=a^2$. Since $\\nabla\\eta\\ne0$ on C, it is normal to C. There $F=\\nabla\\eta/(2a)$, so F is also normal to C.\n\nThe condition a>0 excludes the origin. Multiplying a nonzero normal vector by the positive scalar 1/(2a) preserves its normal direction."}] [[:step/id #uuid "7da1cd95-a447-52ba-98ee-93ed57cb49e9"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405442 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405644} :step/id #uuid "7da1cd95-a447-52ba-98ee-93ed57cb49e9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405493}}] [[:step/id #uuid "8c51de34-8e91-5cdd-8ba0-e50b0c0da2ad"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405493 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405664} :step/id #uuid "8c51de34-8e91-5cdd-8ba0-e50b0c0da2ad" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405127}}] [[:step/id #uuid "1d95f0eb-29af-5f99-a7a1-aa5baac01532"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405127 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405662} :step/id #uuid "1d95f0eb-29af-5f99-a7a1-aa5baac01532"}] [[:multistep/id #uuid "a5643d60-a09c-5b5b-995a-c6199fd64e65"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405563 :multistep/context "Source question: 2(a)–(c), PDF page 3.\n\nLet $\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\mathbf r/|\\mathbf r|=\\langle x,y\\rangle/\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}$, $\\eta(x,y)=x^2+y^2$, and $C: x^2+y^2=a^2$, with $a>0$." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405442} :multistep/id #uuid "a5643d60-a09c-5b5b-995a-c6199fd64e65" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405127 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405662} :step/id #uuid "1d95f0eb-29af-5f99-a7a1-aa5baac01532"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405442 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405644} :step/id #uuid "7da1cd95-a447-52ba-98ee-93ed57cb49e9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405493}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405493 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405664} :step/id #uuid "8c51de34-8e91-5cdd-8ba0-e50b0c0da2ad" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405127}}]}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "bf010f14-eee4-5ffe-bd4d-12fbe79a20ab"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405563} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "bf010f14-eee4-5ffe-bd4d-12fbe79a20ab" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048923} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049366} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050033} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050149}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405641}] [[:question/id #uuid "eecbf7f9-2e6a-5d87-8343-589852d93d37"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405782 :question/id #uuid "eecbf7f9-2e6a-5d87-8343-589852d93d37" :question/problem "**(a)** Draw F and C in the same coordinate axes." :question/worked-solution "**drawing:** Draw the radius-a circle and equal-length arrows circulating counterclockwise around the origin. At (a,0), (0,a), (−a,0), (0,−a), arrows point up, left, down, right. The field is undefined at the origin.\n\n![Authored tangential field reference](images/5c/5c6173bdda7a93fc42142645d1013b63a881e47510dcde4ea6ae142354a2b7d9.png)\n\n$(-y,x)$ is (x,y) rotated 90 degrees counterclockwise. Its magnitude is $\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}$, so normalization gives unit arrows."}] [[:answer/id #uuid "4ea603fe-d241-5466-9608-090211b3172c"] {:answer/id #uuid "4ea603fe-d241-5466-9608-090211b3172c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405999}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "3c04eab7-0ff1-5353-87ac-e71ec81936d3"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ea603fe-d241-5466-9608-090211b3172c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405999}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405999} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c04eab7-0ff1-5353-87ac-e71ec81936d3" :answer-field/key "dot" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405944}] [[:question/id #uuid "1ea08d95-eb9d-5271-8c2b-dd397fb3369d"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405130 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ea603fe-d241-5466-9608-090211b3172c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405999}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405999} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c04eab7-0ff1-5353-87ac-e71ec81936d3" :answer-field/key "dot" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405944}] :question/id #uuid "1ea08d95-eb9d-5271-8c2b-dd397fb3369d" :question/problem "**(b)** Find $\\nabla\\eta\\cdot F$ and conclude that at every point on C, F is tangent (parallel) to C.\n\nDot product: {{dot}}. Supply the conclusion and justification below." :question/worked-solution "**conclusion:** $\\nabla\\eta\\cdot F=(2x(-y)+2yx)/\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}=0$. On C, $\\nabla\\eta$ is a nonzero normal. Thus F is perpendicular to this normal and tangent to C.\n\nUse the normal to the level curve, not the position of an arrow tip, to establish tangency. Both F and the normal are nonzero on the circle because a>0."}] [[:step/id #uuid "63d730f7-9bf6-5703-9edd-93ef0b6cae4a"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405352 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405782} :step/id #uuid "63d730f7-9bf6-5703-9edd-93ef0b6cae4a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405461}}] [[:step/id #uuid "8485d523-7107-507d-8e13-d151278c31e3"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405461 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405130} :step/id #uuid "8485d523-7107-507d-8e13-d151278c31e3"}] [[:multistep/id #uuid "b5ae2259-aa1c-5659-8da4-06e9ae82ee6b"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405610 :multistep/context "Source question: 3(a)–(b), PDF page 4.\n\nLet $\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\langle-y,x\\rangle/\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}$, $\\eta(x,y)=x^2+y^2$, and $C: x^2+y^2=a^2$, with $a>0$." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405352} :multistep/id #uuid "b5ae2259-aa1c-5659-8da4-06e9ae82ee6b" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405352 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405782} :step/id #uuid "63d730f7-9bf6-5703-9edd-93ef0b6cae4a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405461}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405461 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405130} :step/id #uuid "8485d523-7107-507d-8e13-d151278c31e3"}]}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "987120e0-4212-5cdb-bc05-9d156e59f9de"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405610} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "987120e0-4212-5cdb-bc05-9d156e59f9de" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048923} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048960} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049366} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050033}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405523}] [[:question/id #uuid "33107394-a702-572a-88a7-643e15f33d3a"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405201 :question/id #uuid "33107394-a702-572a-88a7-643e15f33d3a" :question/problem "**(a)** The vectors i and j are unit and orthogonal. Confirm that $\\hat{\\mathbf r}$ and $\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}$ are also unit and orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "**proof:** Both squared norms are $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$. Their dot product is $-\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta+\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta=0$. Thus each has length 1 and they are perpendicular.\n\nCheck both lengths and the dot product; orthogonality alone does not imply unit length."}] [[:question/id #uuid "99fc74a6-7d3f-54e2-a15c-0c3e107e6a51"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405528 :question/id #uuid "99fc74a6-7d3f-54e2-a15c-0c3e107e6a51" :question/problem "**(b)** Using $\\hat{\\mathbf r}=\\cos\\theta\\,\\mathbf i+\\sin\\theta\\,\\mathbf j$ and $\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}=-\\sin\\theta\\,\\mathbf i+\\cos\\theta\\,\\mathbf j$, prove\n\n$$\\mathbf i=\\cos\\theta\\,\\hat{\\mathbf r}-\\sin\\theta\\,\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta},\\qquad\\mathbf j=\\sin\\theta\\,\\hat{\\mathbf r}+\\cos\\theta\\,\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}.$$" :question/worked-solution "**proof:** Expand the first right-hand side: $(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)\\mathbf i+(\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta-\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta)\\mathbf j=\\mathbf i$. Expand the second: $(\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta-\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta)\\mathbf i+(\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta)\\mathbf j=\\mathbf j$.\n\nSubstitute the given basis vectors and collect Cartesian components. Mixed terms cancel and squared sine/cosine terms sum to 1."}] [[:step/id #uuid "9efe47ab-9494-5878-a7df-71ccedd3dca6"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405545 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405201} :step/id #uuid "9efe47ab-9494-5878-a7df-71ccedd3dca6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405449}}] [[:step/id #uuid "808c12e7-4aaf-5484-b1e5-96fad9e2715e"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405449 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405528} :step/id #uuid "808c12e7-4aaf-5484-b1e5-96fad9e2715e"}] [[:multistep/id #uuid "880e33b4-548c-5f00-a2dc-f3f54b6cc045"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405477 :multistep/context "Source question: 4(a)–(b), PDF page 5.\n\n**Unit vectors in polar coordinates.** Consider $P(x,y)$, $\\mathbf r=\\overrightarrow{OP}=\\langle x,y\\rangle=\\langle r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta\\rangle$, the unit circle centered at P, and\n\n$$\\mathbf i=\\langle1,0\\rangle,\\quad\\mathbf j=\\langle0,1\\rangle,\\quad\\hat{\\mathbf r}=\\langle\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta\\rangle,\\quad\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}=\\langle-\\sin\\theta,\\cos\\theta\\rangle.$$\n\n![Source polar unit vectors at P](images/35/35a19c56fb5bee3177ff22b713fb8f5b30ea312559b5a1024abcc8360deb2b9e.png)" :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405545} :multistep/id #uuid "880e33b4-548c-5f00-a2dc-f3f54b6cc045" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405449 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405528} :step/id #uuid "808c12e7-4aaf-5484-b1e5-96fad9e2715e"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405545 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405201} :step/id #uuid "9efe47ab-9494-5878-a7df-71ccedd3dca6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405449}}]}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "bfbe6d4f-83b5-54ce-ba13-ee27320a2076"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405477} :assigned-problem/id #uuid "bfbe6d4f-83b5-54ce-ba13-ee27320a2076" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048960} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049366} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050142}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405646}] [[:answer/id #uuid "8a489cd9-5c44-5fcb-9ef1-af26bb86f0b9"] {:answer/id #uuid "8a489cd9-5c44-5fcb-9ef1-af26bb86f0b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "r\\hat{\\mathbf r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406104}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "7b238213-a87b-5d97-b876-0fe9625f7bac"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a489cd9-5c44-5fcb-9ef1-af26bb86f0b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "r\\hat{\\mathbf r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406104}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406104} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b238213-a87b-5d97-b876-0fe9625f7bac" :answer-field/key "polar" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406067}] [[:question/id #uuid "2cc5e181-42e1-5d32-8756-f85d19a09fed"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405181 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a489cd9-5c44-5fcb-9ef1-af26bb86f0b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "r\\hat{\\mathbf r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406104}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406104} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b238213-a87b-5d97-b876-0fe9625f7bac" :answer-field/key "polar" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406067}] :question/id #uuid "2cc5e181-42e1-5d32-8756-f85d19a09fed" :question/problem "**(a)** $\\mathbf F=\\langle x,y\\rangle=x\\mathbf i+y\\mathbf j$.\n\nPolar form: {{polar}}. Explain how the result agrees with the field plot." :question/worked-solution "**interpretation:** The radial coefficient is $x\\cos\\theta+y\\sin\\theta=r$, and the angular coefficient is $-x\\sin\\theta+y\\cos\\theta=0$. It points outward with length r.\n\nThe radial coefficient is $x\\cos\\theta+y\\sin\\theta=r$, and the angular coefficient is $-x\\sin\\theta+y\\cos\\theta=0$. It points outward with length r. Use $x=r\\cos\\theta$, $y=r\\sin\\theta$ and the basis identities from 4(b). Polar directions require r>0; in (a) and (c), the Cartesian field extends to the zero vector at the origin."}] [[:answer/id #uuid "37345573-56ce-58d5-9509-dbe0765c8337"] {:answer/id #uuid "37345573-56ce-58d5-9509-dbe0765c8337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\hat{\\mathbf r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405933}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "d5e6ea38-705a-5319-a8dd-cb1fe1faa355"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37345573-56ce-58d5-9509-dbe0765c8337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\hat{\\mathbf r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405933}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405933} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5e6ea38-705a-5319-a8dd-cb1fe1faa355" :answer-field/key "polar" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406244}] [[:question/id #uuid "b656e2fd-9aeb-5597-87ec-b0770c4f9451"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405613 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37345573-56ce-58d5-9509-dbe0765c8337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\hat{\\mathbf r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405933}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405933} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5e6ea38-705a-5319-a8dd-cb1fe1faa355" :answer-field/key "polar" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406244}] :question/id #uuid "b656e2fd-9aeb-5597-87ec-b0770c4f9451" :question/problem "**(b)** $\\mathbf F=\\frac{\\langle x,y\\rangle}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}\\mathbf i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}\\mathbf j$.\n\nPolar form: {{polar}}. Explain how the result agrees with the field plot." :question/worked-solution "**interpretation:** Divide the result of (a) by r for r>0. It is radial outward with constant unit length and is undefined at the origin.\n\nDivide the result of (a) by r for r>0. It is radial outward with constant unit length and is undefined at the origin. Use $x=r\\cos\\theta$, $y=r\\sin\\theta$ and the basis identities from 4(b). Polar directions require r>0; in (a) and (c), the Cartesian field extends to the zero vector at the origin."}] [[:answer/id #uuid "48d3494b-a2b0-58d9-afaa-a338e34afeea"] {:answer/id #uuid "48d3494b-a2b0-58d9-afaa-a338e34afeea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "r\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405983}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "308f2303-70df-57c5-a16b-d2ff549870d8"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48d3494b-a2b0-58d9-afaa-a338e34afeea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "r\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405983}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405983} :answer-field/id #uuid "308f2303-70df-57c5-a16b-d2ff549870d8" :answer-field/key "polar" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405928}] [[:question/id #uuid "665e3941-44ad-5e1a-9a1b-b2b2a52b1ef8"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405361 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48d3494b-a2b0-58d9-afaa-a338e34afeea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "r\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405983}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405983} :answer-field/id #uuid "308f2303-70df-57c5-a16b-d2ff549870d8" :answer-field/key "polar" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405928}] :question/id #uuid "665e3941-44ad-5e1a-9a1b-b2b2a52b1ef8" :question/problem "**(c)** $\\mathbf F=\\langle-y,x\\rangle=-y\\mathbf i+x\\mathbf j$.\n\nPolar form: {{polar}}. Explain how the result agrees with the field plot." :question/worked-solution "**interpretation:** The radial coefficient $-y\\cos\\theta+x\\sin\\theta$ is 0; the angular coefficient $y\\sin\\theta+x\\cos\\theta$ is r. It circulates counterclockwise with length r.\n\nThe radial coefficient $-y\\cos\\theta+x\\sin\\theta$ is 0; the angular coefficient $y\\sin\\theta+x\\cos\\theta$ is r. It circulates counterclockwise with length r. Use $x=r\\cos\\theta$, $y=r\\sin\\theta$ and the basis identities from 4(b). Polar directions require r>0; in (a) and (c), the Cartesian field extends to the zero vector at the origin."}] [[:answer/id #uuid "fa442124-779a-5710-bd9c-64bc494479e4"] {:answer/id #uuid "fa442124-779a-5710-bd9c-64bc494479e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406322}] [[:answer-field/id #uuid "231cb6d4-e736-503b-9586-e32f8ce0cc47"] {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa442124-779a-5710-bd9c-64bc494479e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406322}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406322} :answer-field/id #uuid "231cb6d4-e736-503b-9586-e32f8ce0cc47" :answer-field/key "polar" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405901}] [[:question/id #uuid "c857505f-9e20-54e3-963b-ca064f545faa"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405668 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa442124-779a-5710-bd9c-64bc494479e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406322}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406322} :answer-field/id #uuid "231cb6d4-e736-503b-9586-e32f8ce0cc47" :answer-field/key "polar" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405901}] :question/id #uuid "c857505f-9e20-54e3-963b-ca064f545faa" :question/problem "**(d)** $\\mathbf F=\\frac{\\langle-y,x\\rangle}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}=\\frac{-y}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}\\mathbf i+\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}\\mathbf j$.\n\nPolar form: {{polar}}. Explain how the result agrees with the field plot." :question/worked-solution "**interpretation:** Divide (c) by r for r>0. The field follows increasing angle with unit length and is undefined at the origin.\n\nDivide (c) by r for r>0. The field follows increasing angle with unit length and is undefined at the origin. Use $x=r\\cos\\theta$, $y=r\\sin\\theta$ and the basis identities from 4(b). Polar directions require r>0; in (a) and (c), the Cartesian field extends to the zero vector at the origin."}] [[:step/id #uuid "6ed9d1e2-3d21-5e7d-9c44-7795c0743974"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405393 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405181} :step/id #uuid "6ed9d1e2-3d21-5e7d-9c44-7795c0743974" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405050}}] [[:step/id #uuid "00864a11-4675-58f9-8705-75378908ae67"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405050 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405613} :step/id #uuid "00864a11-4675-58f9-8705-75378908ae67" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405643}}] [[:step/id #uuid "bf287703-28d3-587f-88ea-a957822f9aed"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405643 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405361} :step/id #uuid "bf287703-28d3-587f-88ea-a957822f9aed" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405082}}] [[:step/id #uuid "0a0161a4-8775-5c8c-8d6d-20a81ee04a00"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405082 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405668} :step/id #uuid "0a0161a4-8775-5c8c-8d6d-20a81ee04a00"}] [[:multistep/id #uuid "90720a6d-ddb7-5303-9b25-3a4c14c8c708"] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405505 :multistep/context "Source question: 5(a)–(d), PDF page 6.\n\nUse Problem 4(b) to express each field entirely in $r,\\theta,\\hat{\\mathbf r},\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}$. Treat the unit vectors as directions of increasing r and θ and reflect on whether the results make sense in the field plots." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405393} :multistep/id #uuid "90720a6d-ddb7-5303-9b25-3a4c14c8c708" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405050 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405613} :step/id #uuid "00864a11-4675-58f9-8705-75378908ae67" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405643}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405082 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405668} :step/id #uuid "0a0161a4-8775-5c8c-8d6d-20a81ee04a00"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405393 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405181} :step/id #uuid "6ed9d1e2-3d21-5e7d-9c44-7795c0743974" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405050}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405643 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405361} :step/id #uuid "bf287703-28d3-587f-88ea-a957822f9aed" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405082}}]}] [[:assigned-problem/id #uuid "26bdee27-1cd8-5c63-a407-5021a3ad5be4"] {:assigned-problem/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405505} :assigned-problem/id #